# DTOs and Validation

## File Naming

- Files: **kebab-case** — `create-store.dto.ts`, `filter-user.dto.ts`, `update-sale.dto.ts`
- Classes: **PascalCase** with suffix `Dto` — `CreateStoreDto`, `FilterUserDto`

## class-validator Decorators

- Use explicit decorators: `@IsString()`, `@IsEmail()`, `@IsOptional()`, `@IsUUID()`, `@IsEnum()`, `@IsInt()`, `@Min()`, `@Max()`, etc.
- Avoid `any`; use concrete types or `Record<string, unknown>` when structure is dynamic.
- Optional fields: apply `@IsOptional()` before other decorators.
- Nested objects: `@ValidateNested()` + `@Type(() => NestedDto)`.

## Mapped Types

- `PartialType(CreateDto)` for Update DTOs (all fields optional)
- `PickType(CreateDto, ['field1', 'field2'])` to pick fields
- `OmitType(CreateDto, ['id'])` to exclude fields
- Import from `@nestjs/mapped-types` or `@nestjs/swagger` depending on Swagger usage

## Example

```typescript
export class CreateStoreDto {
  @IsString()
  @MinLength(1)
  name: string;

  @IsOptional()
  @ValidateNested()
  @Type(() => CreateLocationDto)
  location?: CreateLocationDto;
}
```
